cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this software or its results, please cite the paper below."
title: "Market Making with Persistent Flow Imbalance and Alpha"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Moret"
    given-names: "Felipe"
    affiliation: "Scuola Normale Superiore, Pisa"
  - family-names: "Lillo"
    given-names: "Fabrizio"
    affiliation: "Scuola Normale Superiore, Pisa"
abstract: >-
  Adapts the CARA/GLFT market-making benchmark to persistent order flow through
  three increasingly realistic models: a persistent order-flow imbalance with a
  martingale reference price, a fast-alpha model in which the imbalance
  generates a short-lived price drift, and a slow-regime extension that
  separates transient imbalance from persistent directional pressure.  Each
  model keeps the tractable inventory structure of GLFT and yields closed-form
  quoting approximations that skew the benchmark quotes in response to observed
  flow; common-path simulations compare them with the numerical reduced HJB
  policies.
keywords:
  - market making
  - order-flow imbalance
  - adverse selection
  - Hamilton-Jacobi-Bellman
  - Cole-Hopf
  - regime switching
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/felipemoret77/flow-imbalance-market-making"
